<title>UK: Severn Trent up after earnings, buyback news.</title>
<headline>Severn Trent up after earnings, buyback news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Severn Trent were indicated higher on Tuesday after the British water company said it planned to buy back up to 10 percent of its shares and announced first-half profits in line with expectations.</p>
<p>Severn Trent shares were marked 10p or 1.5 percent higher at 680p while the broader market was up by almost one percent. Volumes remained modest.</p>
<p>The company said pretax profits before exceptional items rose to 201.5 million pounds in the first half from 189 million a year earlier. It said the share buyback would be carried out &quot;as soon as is appropriate.&quot;</p>
